---
import BaseLayout from "../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
import PageHero from "../components/PageHero.astro";
---

<BaseLayout
  title="About Sift"
  description="Why Sift is built around careful questions, visible uncertainty, and restaurant staff confirmation for people with food allergies and their caregivers."
  path="/about"
  schemaType="AboutPage"
>
  <PageHero
    title="Built for the questions menus leave unanswered."
    description="Sift helps people with food allergies and their caregivers turn a menu into a more useful conversation with restaurant staff."
    compact
  />

  <section class="content-section">
    <div class="shell">
      <div class="section-heading">
        <h2>A clearer next step at the table</h2>
        <p>
          Restaurant menus are written to describe dishes, not every ingredient, substitution, preparation
          surface, or cross-contact possibility. Sift is designed for that gap.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div class="prose">
        <p>
          A diner or caregiver selects a menu photo and an allergy profile. Sift reviews the visible menu
          information, surfaces possible concerns and common hidden-risk patterns, and prepares questions that
          can be confirmed with restaurant staff.
        </p>
        <p>
          The result is not a verdict. It is a structured way to notice what may matter, understand what remains
          unknown, and decide what to ask before ordering.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="content-section content-section--tint">
    <div class="shell">
      <div class="section-heading">
        <h2>What guides the product</h2>
        <p>Sift is built around a narrow, protective role: help people prepare better questions without replacing their judgment.</p>
      </div>

      <div class="principle-grid">
        <article class="principle-card">
          <h2>Start with what is visible</h2>
          <p>
            Sift works from the menu image and profile a person provides. It distinguishes visible information
            from inferences and from details the menu cannot answer.
          </p>
        </article>
        <article class="principle-card">
          <h2>Treat uncertainty as useful</h2>
          <p>
            An unclear image or incomplete description should lead to a retake or a staff question—not a confident
            guess.
          </p>
        </article>
        <article class="principle-card">
          <h2>Keep people in the decision</h2>
          <p>
            The diner, caregiver, restaurant staff, and qualified healthcare professionals each know things an app
            cannot. Sift supports that conversation.
          </p>
        </article>
        <article class="principle-card">
          <h2>Earn trust through limits</h2>
          <p>
            Reliability means showing what was checked, using conservative language, and being direct about what
            cannot be verified from a menu.
          </p>
        </article>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="content-section">
    <div class="shell prose">
      <h2>Questions, not guarantees</h2>
      <p>
        Sift cannot inspect a kitchen, verify a recipe, confirm a supplier change, or rule out cross-contact. It is
        not a medical device and does not provide medical advice, diagnosis, or treatment.
      </p>
      <p>
        Always confirm ingredients, preparation, and cross-contact with restaurant staff before ordering,
        especially for severe allergies. Follow the care and emergency guidance provided by qualified healthcare
        professionals.
      </p>
      <p>
        Read more about <a href="/how-it-works">how Sift works</a>, our <a href="/reliability">reliability approach</a>,
        and the product's <a href="/safety">safety boundaries</a>.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
